cff-version: 1.2.0
title: chematic
message: "If you use chematic in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Tanabe"
    given-names: "Kentaro"
    name-suffix: "(kent-tokyo)"
repository-code: https://github.com/kent-tokyo/chematic
url: https://kent-tokyo.github.io/chematic/
abstract: >-
  A pure-Rust cheminformatics toolkit with Python, WebAssembly, and MCP
  interfaces. Provides SMILES parsing, molecular descriptors, fingerprints,
  substructure search, 3D coordinate generation, and AI agent integration.
  The default build is pure Rust; exact standard InChI is available through
  an optional vendored C FFI feature.
keywords:
  - cheminformatics
  - rust
  - python
  - wasm
  - chemistry
  - machine-learning
  - drug-discovery
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.5
date-released: "2026-09-05"
